    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nA3 BER | SOUTH-FACING REAR GARDEN | QUIET CUL-DE-SAC | 3 BED | ENSUITE | AIR-TO-WATER HEAT PUMP | UNDERFLOOR HEAT | EXCELLENT CONDITION | HIGH QUALITY FINISHES | ATTIC FOR CONVERSION(SUBJECT TO PP) | PRIVATE DRIVEWAY \n\nNo.43 Mill View is a beautifully presented, modern three bedroom home, conveniently located in a quiet cul de sac within the newly built and highly sought after Ballinglanna development. This stunning home arrives to the market in tasteful decorative condition with modern finishes throughout. The accommodation is spread over two floors and includes a generous living space, a high quality, modern and bright fully fitted kitchen with elegant stone worktops, and three well-sized bedrooms.\n\nThis home consists of a welcoming entrance hall providing access to the guest WC, a comfortable living room and a generous kitchen/dining area with access to the rear garden. A practical utility room completes the ground floor accommodation. Moving up the stairs, a bright landing provides access to three generously sized bedrooms, one of which benefits from its own private ensuite, a family bathroom and a convenient hot press storage cupboard.\n\nExternally, there is a cobble lock driveway to the front of the property providing off street parking. To the rear, a private south facing garden and patio offers a wonderful outdoor space, bathed in sunshine all day long and late into the evenings — perfect for outdoor living, entertaining and relaxing.\n\nThis property has been built to an excellent A3 BER standard and is equipped with an air to water heat pump, digital thermostat-controlled underfloor heating on the ground floor and high output radiators on the first floor. The home is Smart Home ready, keeping running costs low and offering everyday convenience, and further benefits from an air filtration system for a healthy home environment.\n\nNo.43 Mill View is only a 5-minute drive to Creastfield Shopping Centre which offers all local and social amenities. The Dunkettle interchange is easily accessible from here and offers routes to the city centre, Cork Airport, Little Island and Ringaskiddy to name a few.\n\nThis property will appeal to many home buyers, given its spacious layout, excellent condition and convenient location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 5.04m x 1.97m\nA bright and welcoming entrance hall giving access to all downstairs accommodation which features beautiful herringbone flooring and storage space under the stairs.\n\nLiving Room - 4.98m x 3.69m\nThis is a spacious reception room to the front of the home with a large bay window filling the room with natural light. The room benefits from herringbone flooring and a built-in electric fireplace.\n\nKitchen/Dining Area - 5.05m x 4.19m\nThis open-plan area is located to the rear of the property. The kitchen is well-fitted with both floor and eye-level units, tiled splash back, marble counter tops and a selection of premium kitchen appliances. The dining area is an open reception space overlooking the rear garden through glass French doors and features tiled flooring.\n\nUtillity - 1.49m x 1.24m\nAccessed directly off the kitchen/dining area, this separate utility room is fully equipped with a top of the line complement of appliances, giving true move-in-ready appeal. The room is plumbed for washer and dryer and features tiled flooring.\n\nGuest W.C - 1.47m x 1.46m\nA tastefully decorated, fully tiled two-piece suite complete with built in storage, making excellent use of the space.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.32m x 3.64m\nA large double bedroom to the front of the home with large bay window filling the room with natural light, finished with pure wool carpeting and fitted with high end Venetian and electric blackout window blinds. This primary bedroom benefits from its own private ensuite.\n\nEnsuite - 1.01m x 2.97m\nPart tiled ensuite featuring a large shower unit with high quality frameless saloon style doors and a black rainwater shower head. The ensuite also has a large window for natural light and ventilation.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.66m x 3.46m\nLarge double bedroom overlooking the rear garden with built-in wardrobes and pure wool carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.88m x 2.66m\nGenerous single bedroom to the rear of the home with carpet flooring.\n\nBathroom - 2.41m x 2.06m\nA beautifully appointed, part tiled three-piece suite featuring an extra deep bath, a rainwater shower and wooden window shutters, creating a private, warm and luxurious feel while benefiting from a window for natural light and ventilation.\n\nAttic - \nSuitable for conversion.\n\n"
      },
